  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: af71b7085f909a146a92198d3b044f71, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  noteTitle: Ideal gas
  noteContent: "An ideal gas is a simplified model of a real gas. It assumes that
    gas particles:\n\nHave no volume of their own\n\nDon't attract or repel each
    other\n\nMove in constant, random motion\n\nCollide elastically (no energy lost)\n\nThis
    model helps us understand how gases behave under different conditions.\n\nThe
    behavior of an ideal gas is described by the Ideal Gas Law:\nPV = nRT\n\nWhere:\n\nP
    = Pressure (in Pascals)\n\nV = Volume (in liters or cubic meters)\n\nn = Amount
    of gas (in moles)\n\nR = Gas constant (\u2248 8.31 J/mol\xB7K)\n\nT = Temperature
    (in Kelvin)"
